	)	)
	(text "Task 12 -- 5x MHF4 (SMT receptacle) -> SMA (edge jack) RF antenna breakouts. Pure passive: signal center pin (pin 1) net-to-net per pair, shield/ground pin (pin 2) tied to GND at both ends. Nets ANT0/ANT1/ANT2/ANT3/GNSS, netclass RF_50 (patterns \"ANT*\"/\"GNSS\", declared project-file Task 3, unmodified here -- verified names match). Refdes remap (brief's placeholder J5-J9 MHF4 / J10-J14 SMA, offset-5 pairing, predates the current project state): J5=Qwiic and J7=Spare (mcu.kicad_sch), J8=magjack (ethernet.kicad_sch) already claimed those numbers. Continuing numerically from J8 with adjacent (N/N+1) MHF4/SMA pairs instead: J9/J10=ANT0, J11/J12=ANT1, J13/J14=ANT2, J15/J16=ANT3, J17/J18=GNSS -- see task-12-report.md for the full table. Symbol choice: stock Connector:Conn_Coaxial (pin 1=In/signal, pin 2=Ext/shield) used for BOTH connector classes rather than authoring custom MHF4/SMA symbols. No exact-MPN stock footprint exists for the sourced parts (TE CONMHF4-SMD-G-T / BAT Wireless BWSMA-KE-Z001, per docs/sourcing.md), so pin numbering was verified against the closest same-manufacturer-class stock footprints instead: U.FL_Hirose_U.FL-R-SMT-1_Vertical.kicad_mod (MHF4/U.FL-class SMD receptacle: pad 1=signal, pad 2 x2=shield tabs) and SMA_BAT_Wireless_BWSMA-KWE-Z001.kicad_mod (same BAT Wireless SMA-edge family, differs only in mount-style suffix KWE vs KE: pad 1=roundrect/signal, pad 2 x4=shield tabs). Both match Conn_Coaxial's pin1=signal/pin2=shield numbering exactly; real footprints for these exact MPNs are authored/linked at Task 14, not this task."
		(at 10 8 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
		(uuid "aeb40839-e840-479d-9268-f57006591c82")
	)
	(text "50 ohm CPWG, via-fenced, keep runs short -- see plan Task 18; label silks ANT0-3/GNSS at both connectors. (ASCII-substituted for the project's plain-ASCII sheet convention: \"ohm\" for the Omega symbol, \"--\" for the em dash -- semantics unchanged.)"
		(at 10 145 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
		(uuid "c44d228b-84cd-448b-9de2-3c0a688e0441")
	)
